<title>FINLAND: HELSINKI BOND MKT TRADING HOURS REMAIN UNCHANGED.</title>
<headline>HELSINKI BOND MKT TRADING HOURS REMAIN UNCHANGED.</headline>
<dateline>HELSINKI 1996-11-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>Interbank traders agreed in a meeting on Friday to keep bond market opening hours unchanged. The bond market will remain open between 1000/0800 GMT and 1600/1400 GMT, they said.</p>
<p>&quot;There was neither the need nor interest in extend trading hours,&quot; one senior dealer said.</p>
<p>After-hours trading will still be possible after the closing at 1600/1400 GMT, market sources said.</p>
<p>Foreign exchange trading hours were extended until 1715/1415 GMT from 1600/1400 GMT on October 14.</p>
<p>The next primary dealer meeting will be held in December.</p>
<p>-- Veera Heinonen, Helsinki newsroom + 358 - 0 - 680 50 240</p>
</text>
